<title>USA: CSX sees non-dilutive merger.</title>
<headline>CSX sees non-dilutive merger.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>CSX Corp chairman John Snow said the company's proposed merger with Conrail Inc would be non-dilutive from the first year.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be non-dilutive from the first year on,&quot; Snow told a telephone news conference on the merger. He attributed the prognosis to strong cash flow projections in the merger. He said the tender offer for 40 percent of Conrail's shares would be financed.</p>
<p>The two companies said in their merger announcement the deal would be accretive to earnings per share in its second year. Completion is targeted for late 1997.</p>
</text>
